watch-pin-held — watch-pin-dead one tick later: watch.hold already names alpha.

Same world as watch-pin-dead (pinned alpha, third failed probe, network clear,
the direct TCP connect to 203.0.113.10:443 timing out), with the hold already
stamped. Expected: one short line, "pinned server alpha still dead (… holding,
not reloading …)", no audit line, watch.hold byte for byte as it was, and the
streak at 3.

Also the `status` case: with the hold naming the server still pinned, status
prints an `escape:` row saying alpha is dead since the stamp and what to do.
And the `use beta` and `reload` cases: a new selection and any reload end the
hold — both sides remove watch.hold (the config-tree compare catches a side
that keeps it).
